= Economic evaluation of the effects of manual therapy for knee osteoarthritis: Study protocol
#smallcaps[Published]\ 17 May 2024

#smallcaps[Citation]\ #eval("Pryymachenko Y, Wilson R, Abbott JH, Chapple C. Economic evaluation of the effects of manual therapy for knee osteoarthritis: Study protocol. OSF, 17 May 2024. Available at: https://osf.io/arn9v/", mode: "markup")

=== Abstract
Manual therapy (MT) has been shown to be a cost-effective treatment for
knee or hip osteoarthritis (OA), one of the most common and debilitating
health conditions. However, the optimal dose of MT has not been identified.
The Opti-OK trial was a three-arm superiority randomised controlled trial
investigating whether frequency of MT (one of the aspects of dosage)
influences clinical and cost-effectiveness at six-months for people with
knee OA. In this paper, we outline the protocol for an economic evaluation
to be conducted in conjunction with the Opti-OK trial.

